  "limitations": [
    "One fresh direct Telnet process executes only its immutable region/saved-edge sequence; every phase is observed before the next input or resize.",
    "Active cases preserve shrink-only and separate upper/lower CUP stages; saved-primary-edge preserves a separate return-only stage before X.",
    "Saved-primary-edge stage 3 is unmodified return; active CUP stages are explicit controls, never the pre-action cursor. No LF is sent.",
    "Document markers, protocol DSR and visible rectangles remain different observations; no internal storage or addressing policy is inferred.",
    "DSR is bounded independently to row 1..200 and column 1..500; a reply beyond the current 61-column grid is preserved, not rejected as a viewport mismatch.",
    "The finite allowlist admits literal column-6 sentinel/column-10 frame words, column-1 controls, declared edge writes, fixed-width fragments and trailing blanks. Missing markers or inseparable controls remain observations, not semantic failures.",
    "Only 91x20 -> 61x20 -> 91x20 is covered, with no full grid, local-shell transport, reliability repetition or performance acceptance.",
    "Raw document text, paths, process identifiers, profiles, resources and provider diagnostics remain private."
  ]
